Q: How to configure logging provider with dependency injection for .NET library A: <p>Actually, the mistake you are making is simply not resolving the class the logger is being injected into.  you need to make sure that in the startup file, you configure Logging for service injection:</p>
<pre><code>services.AddLogging();
</code></pre>
<p>And in the class you are injecting, just do basic constructor injection, typing ILogger to the hosting class:</p>
<pre><code>private readonly ILogger&lt;DoIt&gt; _logger;

public DoIt(ILogger&lt;DoIt&gt; logger)
{
   _logger = logger;
}
</code></pre>

